{
  "_readme": "The one list of conditions a workflow step's when.condition may hold, and of the ones it may not. Read by the plugin's runner test (scripts/tests/workflow-conditions.sh) and by DevStride's own parser specs, so the parsers cannot drift. Grammar: an optional leading !, then one predicate: review-path:fast or review-path:pull-request; item-tag:<name> and item-work-type:<name> (1 to 100 characters, the rest of the text including colons, no control characters, no leading or trailing space); touches:<glob> (1 to 150 characters, no white space or control characters, no branch date token such as <YY-MM-DD>, no trailing [-n]); has-repository (no argument); step-verdict:<step id>:<WORD> (a step id [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*, a verdict word [A-Z][A-Z0-9 -]*). At most 200 characters in all. No and, or, parentheses or free text. valid is the grammar's answer alone: whether a step-verdict names an earlier step and a word its contract allows is checked against the definition, not here. reason is for people and is never compared.",
